{
  "schema": "sim-xp/playbook@2",
  "meta": {
    "id": "postgres-queue-load-test",
    "title": "Postgres as a queue: the load test that found the wall",
    "story": "A team runs its job queue on a Postgres table with SKIP LOCKED and ramps a load test to see where it breaks. The first two stages pass easily, then something quiet starts piling up. Compressed: 1 s ≈ 4 s.",
    "duration_s": 330,
    "tags": [
      "postgres",
      "queue",
      "load-test",
      "vacuum",
      "dramatized"
    ],
    "clock": {
      "scale": 4
    },
    "layout": {
      "columns": 3,
      "rows": 3
    },
    "background": [
      {
        "title": "The system",
        "body": "checkout enqueues jobs into a jobs table in Postgres. 20 workers claim 50 rows at a time with SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, process them and delete them. No broker, one less thing to run."
      },
      {
        "title": "How it normally works",
        "body": "Every claim and delete leaves dead row versions behind. Autovacuum removes them, but only versions no open transaction could still see. Normally that is milliseconds after the delete, so the table stays small."
      },
      {
        "title": "Today",
        "body": "A load test ramps from 200 to 800 to 1,500 jobs/s to find the limit. At some point in the run, a scheduled weekly export also starts on the same database."
      }
    ],
    "cast": [
      {
        "name": "k6 load test",
        "role": "ramps enqueue rate in stages"
      },
      {
        "name": "enqueue-api",
        "role": "inserts jobs, 100 DB connections shared"
      },
      {
        "name": "jobs-db",
        "role": "Postgres holding the jobs table"
      },
      {
        "name": "worker-pool",
        "role": "20 workers claiming and deleting jobs"
      },
      {
        "name": "autovacuum",
        "role": "cleans dead row versions"
      },
      {
        "name": "weekly-export",
        "role": "cron job reading the jobs table"
      }
    ],
    "watch": [
      {
        "label": "Queue depth",
        "normal": "normal: under 500"
      },
      {
        "label": "Dequeue p99",
        "normal": "normal: under 20 ms"
      },
      {
        "label": "Dead tuples",
        "normal": "normal: tens of thousands"
      }
    ],
    "learn": [
      "why a queue table is hard on Postgres",
      "what holds vacuum back, and why CPU hides it",
      "how a slow dequeue turns into enqueue errors"
    ]
  },
  "components": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "loadgen",
        "label": "k6 load test",
        "kind": "load generator",
        "details": [
          {
            "label": "Offered load",
            "metric": "enq_rate"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "api",
        "label": "enqueue-api",
        "kind": "service",
        "details": [
          {
            "label": "Enqueue errors",
            "metric": "errors"
          },
          {
            "label": "Accepted rate",
            "metric": "enq_rate"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "db",
        "label": "jobs-db",
        "kind": "postgres",
        "details": [
          {
            "label": "Queue depth",
            "metric": "depth"
          },
          {
            "label": "Dequeue p99",
            "metric": "deq_p99"
          },
          {
            "label": "Dead tuples",
            "metric": "dead_tup"
          },
          {
            "label": "Table size",
            "metric": "table_gb"
          },
          {
            "label": "CPU",
            "metric": "db_cpu"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "workers",
        "label": "worker-pool",
        "kind": "20 consumers",
        "details": [
          {
            "label": "Completed",
            "metric": "done_rate"
          },
          {
            "label": "Connections in use",
            "metric": "conns"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "vacuum",
        "label": "autovacuum",
        "kind": "postgres daemon",
        "details": [
          {
            "label": "Dead tuples",
            "metric": "dead_tup"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "report",
        "label": "weekly-export",
        "kind": "cron job",
        "details": [
